# S5-07 canonical `norandmaps` same-input replay controls

Date: 2026-11-16

## Scope

Repeat each run from the canonical `norandmaps` automatic N=2 diagnostic as a
direct invocation, reusing the exact run-specific nonce, kernel/initramfs/ACPI
inputs, 128 MiB profile, 3-billion instruction budget, and schema-v5 sidecar
capture. This checks repeatability under identical guest-visible inputs. The
controls are diagnostic, not a counted unique-nonce series or acceptance
evidence.

Both invocations used runner SHA-256
`d0e3be4b345cb1ce4b2b5e72c721630ab098641b29e77816b13fdd2e13c4251f`, built
from source revision `b6d5e7803c63f9b586776a1f5493440fd3526efb`.

```sh
target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --nonce OD518e87e0fcdbcc3a00000e27000000000 \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --ram-mib 128 --out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-norandmaps-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0001.json \
  --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode \
  --linux-norandmaps \
  --execution-observations-out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-norandmaps-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0001-execution-observations.json

target/release/od-runner linux-direct \
  --nonce OD518e87f2156c65b180000e27000000001 \
  --expected-vmlinuz-sha256 9f55ef7253055a9cf68f8a04323c93dead2fca617386d842fbde9ca7b178b27e \
  --expected-initramfs-sha256 65acac38cd4c791154f33179fe2c9f2103dd7fdec51aacfd969ab4d9eb0aedb7 \
  --expected-acpi-manifest-hash 2bd690ae0817705b1b128675f9628dd7212fee74ab97c88da3599a1ae8e398f2 \
  --vmlinuz /Users/senya/projects/open_desktop/work/stage4/linux-7.0.0-38.38/vmlinuz-7.0.0-38-generic \
  --initramfs work/stage4/initramfs/initramfs.cpio \
  --acpi-blob tests/fixtures/guest/stage4/acpi_blob/stage4_acpi_blob.bin \
  --ram-mib 128 --out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-norandmaps-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0002.json \
  --run --budget 3000000000 --set-cpl0 --cpuid-profile stage4a --user-mode \
  --linux-norandmaps \
  --execution-observations-out work/stage5/s5-07-canonical-norandmaps-same-input-replay-n2-20261116-a/run-0002-execution-observations.json
```

## Results

| Source run | Replayed nonce | Retired / stop | Stop equal | UART equal | Sidecar equal |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0001 | `OD518e87e0fcdbcc3a00000e27000000000` | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | yes | yes | yes |
| 0002 | `OD518e87f2156c65b180000e27000000001` | 2,999,999,998 / `budget_exhausted` | yes | yes | yes |

Both replays reported `loaded`, `guest_started=true`, and passed the exact
nonce marker. For each run, the complete machine stop object, UART bytes, and
schema-v5 sidecar are byte-identical to the corresponding automatic-series
run. Runner JSON is also identical after replacing only
`execution_observations_sidecar.path` with a common placeholder.

The controls show that each output from the automatic pair repeats under its
same nonce and guest artifacts. This makes the cross-run variation repeatable
per input, but does not identify which input-dependent state causes it, prove
that the nonce itself is causal, or establish benignity. The strict N=2
comparison remains false; no comparator normalization changed and S5-07
remains blocked/unaccepted.

